# Help documentation (required)

When you add or change **anything operators see or do** in Dynamic Listings, update the in-app help in the **same task** (same PR / same change set). Do not ship UI, routes, or workflows without matching help text.

## Source files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `dl/templates/_help_document.html` | All help sections and TOC links |
| `dl/templates/help_page.html` | Signed-in shell (only if layout/actions change) |
| `dl/templates/help_login.html` | Pre-login shell (only if layout/actions change) |
| `dl/static/css/help.css` | Help-specific layout (bump `?v=` when changed) |
| `dl/static/js/help.js` | Print / PDF (bump `?v=` when changed) |

Content is shared via `_help_document.html`; edit sections there unless you are changing chrome only.

## What triggers a help update

- New dashboard module, route, or navigation item (sidebar, top bar, login footer)
- New or renamed buttons, forms, fields, exports, or **Display** / refresh behavior
- Role, sign-in, or permission changes
- Data model changes that affect how users create/edit records (e.g. Veto prefix/link fields)
- Removed or deprecated features (remove or mark obsolete in help)

## How to update

1. Add or revise numbered sections with stable `id` anchors (kebab-case) in `_help_document.html`.
2. Mirror every new/changed section in the **Contents** `<ol>` at the top of that file.
3. Use **exact UI labels** from the app (`<strong>Update the table</strong>`, etc.).
4. Audience: **operators and admins**, not developers (no env dumps unless troubleshooting).
5. Bump `help.css?v=` / `help.js?v=` in `help_page.html` and `help_login.html` when those assets change.
6. Optionally bump `Document version:` month/year in the help header when content materially changes.

## Checklist before finishing a feature

- [ ] Help describes the new/changed workflow end-to-end
- [ ] TOC includes links to new section ids
- [ ] Export, refresh, and module-specific quirks documented if they changed
- [ ] Troubleshooting updated if users might hit new failure modes

Reference pattern: ISMT `WEB/help.html`; this project uses the app-themed `help_page.html` + `_help_document.html`.
